  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Wisconsin has received $3.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 59,453 awards with an average award size of $65K. Obligations fell 38.3% year over year. Fiscal year obligations by year were $5.8B in FY21, $5.2B in FY22, $5.3B in FY23, $8.9B in FY24, $6.3B in FY25, and $3.9B in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer with $2.3B in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $986M and the Department of Agriculture with $207M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor with $1.9B in obligations, followed by OSHKOSH DEFENSE LLC with $805M and AMTEC CORPORATION with $283M. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the largest industry by obligations with $1.9B, followed by Truck Trailer Manufacturing with $566M and Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing with $307M. All totals are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial.",
