        "body": "Obligations fell 38.3% year over year. Fiscal year obligations show a peak at $8.9B in FY24 and a decline to $3.9B in FY26 to date. Award volume remained substantial with 59,453 awards and an average award size of $65K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Wisconsin?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs dominates buying with $2.3B in obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $986M and the Department of Agriculture with $207M. OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. leads vendors with $1.9B, followed by OSHKOSH DEFENSE LLC with $805M and AMTEC CORPORATION with $283M."
      }
